"L(3, 2, 1)-Labeling of the Square of Cycles (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397438492_L3_2_1-Labeling_of_the_Square_of_Cycles)\nciteturn3search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Crawled: 2 months ago; # L(3, 2, 1)-Labeling of the Square of Cycles ... Image: Request Full-text Paper PDF ... Calamoneri who studied the square of cycles, i.e., circulants $C_n(\\{1,2,n-2,n-1\\})$. ... The L(2,1) and L(3,2,1) labelling number of G, denoted by λ_2,1 (G) and λ_3,2,1 (G) respectively which is the smallest number k such that there is an L(2,1) and L(3,2,1) labelling with maximum label k.\n\n# L(3, 2, 1)-Labeling of the Square of Cycles\n\n  * November 2025\n  * Theoretical Computer Science 1060:115627\n\nDOI:10.1016/j.tcs.2025.115627\n\n  * License\n  * CC BY-NC-ND 4.0\n\nAuthors:\n\nValerio Bianco\n\nValerio Bianco\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nTiziana Calamoneri\n\nTiziana Calamoneri\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nTo read the full-text of this research, you can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nImage: ResearchGate Logo\n\nDiscover the world's research\n\n  * 25+ million members\n  * 160+ million publication pages\n  * 2.3+ billion citations\nJoin for free\n\n## No full-text available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\n## Citations (1)\n\n## References (16)\n\n... Recently, a series of papers on various L(p, q)-labelings of circulants has been published (see [16,17,18]). \nPreprint\n\n  * Jan 2026\n\n  * Přemysl Holub\n  * Martin Kopřiva\n\nAn L(3,2,1)-labeling of a graph G is an assignment f of nonnegative integers to vertices such that \\vert f(x)-f(y)\\vert > 3-\\mbox{dist}_G(x,y) for every pair x,y of vertices of G, where \\mbox{dist}_G(x,y) denotes the distance between x and y in G. The minimum span (i.e., the difference between the largest and the smallest value) among all L(3,2,1)-labelings of G is denoted by $λ_{(3,2,1)}(G)$. In this paper, we study L(3,2,1)-labelings of three classes of circulant graphs. Namely, we investigate $λ_{(3,2,1)}$ of $C_n(\\{1,s_2,n-s_2,n-1\\})$, where $s_2\\in\\{3,4,5\\}$. This paper is a continuation of a recent publication of T. Calamoneri who studied the square of cycles, i.e., circulants $C_n(\\{1,2,n-2,n-1\\})$.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\nL(2,1) and L(3,2,1) Labelling of Certain Star and Wheel Related Graphs\n\nArticle\n\nFull-text available\n\n  * Jun 2020\n\n  * Francis Xavier D\n  * Kins Yenoke\n  * Preethi S\n\nABSTRACT: An L(2,1) and L(3,2,1)-labelling of a graph G is a function from the vertex set V(G) to the set of all non-negative integers such that d(x,y)+|f(x)-f(y)| ≥ 1+k, for k=2 and k=3 respectively. The L(2,1) and L(3,2,1) labelling number of G, denoted by λ_2,1 (G) and λ_3,2,1 (G) respectively which is the smallest number k such that there is an L(2,1) and L(3,2,1) labelling with maximum label k. In this paper, L(2,1) and L(3,2,1)-labelling number of certain star and wheel related graphs were determined.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNew results on radio k -labelings of distance graphs | Request PDF (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/354876125_New_results_on_radio_k_-labelings_of_distance_graphs)\nciteturn3search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.2 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # New results on radio k -labelings of distance graphs ... Aleksander Vesel\n\n# New results on radio k -labelings of distance graphs\n\n  * September 2021\n  * Discrete Applied Mathematics 319(1)\n\nDOI:10.1016/j.dam.2021.09.007\n\nAuthors:\n\nDanilo Korže\n\n  * University of Maribor\n\nZehui Shao\n\nZehui Shao\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nAleksander Vesel\n\n  * University of Maribor\n\n\n## Abstract\n\nA radio k-labeling of a graph G is an assignment of non-negative integers (labels) to the vertices of G such that the absolute value of the difference between the labels of any two distinct vertices u and v is not less than k+1−d(u,v), where d(u,v) denotes the distance between u and v. The radio k-labeling number of G is the minimum span of a radio k-labeling of G. For a given set of integers D={d1,d2,…,dt}, the distance graph G(Z,D), denoted also by D(d1,d2,…,dt), has the set of integers Z as its vertex set, while two distinct vertices i,j∈Z are adjacent in G(Z,D) if and only if |i−j|∈D. Radio k-labelings of three families of distance graphs are considered. Some improved theoretical lower and upper bounds on the radio k-labeling number are presented and some computer-based methods for computing radio k-labelings of these families of graphs are proposed.\n\n\n## Citations (9)\n\n## References (11)\n\n\nRadio Labelings of Distance Graphs\n\nArticle\n\n  * Dec 2013\n  * DISCRETE APPL MATH\n\n  * Roman Cada\n  * Jan Ekstein\n  * Přemysl Holub\n  * Olivier Togni\n\nMotivated by the Channel Assignment Problem, we study radio k-labelings of graphs. A radio k-labeling of a connected graph G is an assignment c of non-negative integers to the vertices of G such that vertical bar c(x) - c(y)vertical bar >= k + 1 - d(x, y). for any two vertices x and y, x not equal y, where d(x, y) is the distance between x and y in G. In this paper, we study radio k-labelings of distance graphs, i.e., graphs with the set Z of integers as vertex set and in which two distinct vertices i, j is an element of Z are adjacent if and only if vertical bar i - j vertical bar is an element of D. We give some lower and upper bounds for radio k-labelings of distance graphs with distance sets D(1, 2,....t), D(1, t) and D(t - 1, t) for any positive integer t > 1.\n\nView--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nL(3,2,1)$-LABELING OF GRAPHS | Request PDF (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/318514409_L321-LABELING_OF_GRAPHS)\nciteturn3search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Image: Request Full-text Paper PDF ... For a graph G = ( V, E ) the L (3, 1, 1)-labeling is a mapping μ from the vertex set V to the set of non-negative integers {0, 1, 2, …} such that | μ ( x ) - μ ( y ) |≥3 if d ( x, y ) =3 and | μ ( x ) - μ ( y ) |≥1 if d ( x, y ) =2 or 3, where d ( x, y ) is the distance between the vertices x and y . λ 3,1,1 ( G ) represents the L (3, 1, 1)-labeling number of the graph G and it is the largest non-negative integer used to label the graph G . In the present article we have studied L (3, 1, 1)-labeling of squares of some simple graphs, namely square of paths ( P n 2 ) , square of complete graphs ( K n 2 ) and square of complete bipartite graphs ( K p , q 2 ) and we obtained good results for these graph classes.\nArticle\n\n# L(3,2,1)$-LABELING OF GRAPHS\n\n  * November 2011\n  * Taiwanese Journal of Mathematics 15(6):2439-2457\n\nDOI:10.11650/twjm/1500406480\n\nAuthors:\n\nMa-Lian Chia\n\n  * Aletheia University\n\nDavid Kuo\n\n  * National Dong Hwa University\n\nHong-ya Liao\n\nHong-ya Liao\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nCian-Hui Yang\n\nCian-Hui Yang\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nShow all 5 authors Hide\n\n## No full-text available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\n## Citations (25)\n\n## References (13)\n\n... O Problema da Rotulação-L(3,2,1) tem sido largamente tratado até então pelo viés da teoria dos grafos e, apesar de avanços teóricos em classes de grafos específicas [Clipperton et al. 2005, Chia et al. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n“保赢一号”产品保单单证作废声明 (https://www.tianan-insurance.com/tianwebsite/2019-05-27/15589271551301519012213ns.pdf)\nciteturn3search12 